# Slow-Burn Chain Blend (Concept Spec)

Base_Alkane_Fuel
  Component: Gasoline-range alkanes
  Fraction: 94–96 % by volume
  Role: Main energy carrier, vaporizes in carburetor.

Ethanol
  Component: CH3CH2OH
  Fraction: 2–3 % by volume
  Role:
    - Co-solvent between aqueous additive and fuel.
    - Lowers flame temperature slightly.
    - Helps carry a trace of water into vapor phase.

Water
  Component: H2O (in additive solution)
  Fraction: 1–2 % by volume (as liquid in tank; part becomes vapor in intake)
  Role:
    - Charge cooling when vaporized.
    - Slows pressure rise and peak temperature.

Aromatic_Salt_Additive_Solution
  Example_Solute: Sodium_Benzoate (C6H5COO⁻ Na⁺)
  Solute_Fraction: ~0.1–0.5 % by volume (dissolved in the water/ethanol microphase)
  Role:
    - Dissolves in water → “saline/aromatic” additive solution.
    - Stays in aqueous/alcohol droplets; does not enter vapor phase.
    - Chemically spectator in combustion; practical effect is negligible on flame speed.

Phase_Behavior
  - In the tank: micro-droplets of water/ethanol + aromatic salt dispersed in alkane.
  - In the carburetor: alkane + ethanol + some water vapor enter the charge.
  - At the flame front: alkane + ethanol + water vapor burn; aromatic salt remains non-volatile residue.
